  "interpretation": "V2 motion-only is the numeric public-window Spell F1 leader at 0.328889; V2 shape-only and shape-plus-motion are close at 0.327273, with overlapping uncertainty ranges. V3 soft stoppage is the more precise D clue. V6 learned signals catch more dead-ball frames but add many false D labels and break up possession spells. V6's learned D overlay was not tested on the V2 motion-only parent. The 0.2433 full-match baseline and these public-window scores use different evaluation sets and cannot be directly compared.",
  "limitations": [
    "Only three public sample matches; weak event-derived frame labels may include uncertain interval timing.",
    "The public BAR-ATH window has 17 spells; its scores can rank methods differently from the full match.",
    "BAR-ATH tracks have no separate referee, no ball height, and anonymous fragments rather than reliable named player identity.",
    "2D geometry cannot prove offside, handball, goal height, or the reason for a stoppage.",
    "Pitch thirds are absolute left/middle/right; attacking/defensive labels require verified direction by half.",
    "Voronoi area is a coarse nearest-player grid, not a complete time-to-intercept pitch-control model.",
    "Public sample files and frame-level outputs remain local under ignored data/."
  ]
